{"step_index":1130,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:11:18Z","thinking":"**Refining Overflow Strategy**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! I noticed `history-grid` lacks overflow in screen-history. If `.screen` has `overflow-y: auto`, the entire history scrolls. Now, I'm trying removing `overflow-y: auto` from `.screen` and moving it to the individual grid classes like `.history-grid`, `.upload-grid`, and `.settings-grid`, to contain scrolling appropriately.\n\n\n**Revisiting Scrolling Behavior**\n\nI'm now reconsidering the scrolling strategy. I had thought `.screen` scrolling was ideal, but now realize there's resistance to that approach. The feedback pointed out that screen-level scrolling may not be flexible. I'm exploring the idea of adapting layout according to screen size, so that the scroll is never on `.screen`, but when the screen size is small, the layout breaks. I'm now exploring how to make sure the layout can gracefully respond to different screen sizes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"lines=open('d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/templates/index.html', encoding='utf-8').readlines(); print('\\\\n'.join([f'{i}: {l.strip()}' for i, l in enumerate(lines) if 'grid' in l]))\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"500","toolAction":"\"Check grids\"","toolSummary":"\"Check grids\""}}]}
